# Commit Message Template
# 
# Format: <type>: <subject>
#
# Type:
#   feat:     New feature
#   fix:      Bug fix
#   docs:     Documentation only changes
#   style:    Code style changes (formatting, semicolons, etc)
#   refactor: Code change that neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature
#   perf:     Performance improvement
#   test:     Adding or updating tests
#   chore:    Changes to build process or auxiliary tools
#
# Subject:
#   - Use imperative mood ("add" not "added" or "adds")
#   - Don't capitalize first letter
#   - No period at the end
#   - Keep under 50 characters
#
# Example:
#   feat: add tab navigation with four main screens
#   fix: update navigation logic to enhance user experience
#   refactor: improve code structure in HomeScreen component
#
# Current commit example (based on your request):
# fix: update lesson visibility logic to enhance user experience in PhaseComponent

# Current changes for Lost & Found QR:
feat: add tab navigation with four beautiful screens

- Created ScanScreen with QR code scanner interface and flash control
- Created RegisterScreen with comprehensive item registration form
- Created MyItemsScreen with stats cards and item management
- Enhanced HomeScreen with gradient design and feature cards
- Implemented TabNavigator with bottom tabs using Lucide icons
- Updated App.tsx to use NavigationContainer
- Fixed TypeScript issues with NativeWind className props
- Added proper type definitions for tab bar icon props

This commit significantly enhances user experience by providing:
- Beautiful, modern UI with gradients and smooth animations
- Intuitive navigation between main features
- Clear visual hierarchy and information architecture
- Consistent design language across all screens
